---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const title = `Terms of Use & Pricing Disclaimers | ${siteConfig.businessName}`;
const description = 'Website terms of use and transparent pricing disclaimers for Staten Island Software.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="section legal-page-section">
    <div class="container legal-container">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <span class="section-tag">Terms & Conditions</span>
        <h1>Terms of Service &amp; SMS Messaging Terms</h1>
        <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: November 21, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content card">
        <h2>1. Website Informational Purpose &amp; Acceptance</h2>
        <p>
          This website is published by Staten Island Software (including Jenkins HQ software products and services), operated by {siteConfig.ownerName}, to describe software engineering, digital tools, web development, and automation services. By accessing this website or opting in to our communications, you agree to these Terms of Service.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Pricing & Non-Binding Estimates</h2>
        <p>
          All pricing listed on this website (including website packages starting at $349, automation starting at $149, custom software starting at $699, and hourly rates) is <strong>introductory and representative starting pricing</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pricing presented on this website does <strong>not</strong> constitute a binding contract or firm offer to complete unspecified work. Every formal client engagement requires a mutually agreed, written scope of work specifying:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Explicit deliverable items and architecture requirements.</li>
          <li>Estimated timeline and project milestone schedules.</li>
          <li>Total fixed project price or agreed hourly rate.</li>
          <li>Specific technical exclusions or third-party license costs.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Independent Contractual Engagement</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting a project inquiry or contacting Staten Island Software does not establish an attorney-client, agency, partnership, or binding development relationship. Development work begins only after both parties agree to project specifications and the initial deposit or milestone payment is confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Code Ownership & Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          Website visitors may not scrape, replicate, or misappropriate the brand assets, trademarked identifiers, or visual assets of Staten Island Software without authorization.
        </p>
        <p>
          For client engagements, intellectual property ownership of custom source code is granted upon receipt of final payment as detailed in each individual project agreement. Pre-existing software libraries, frameworks, and open-source packages remain subject to their respective licenses.
        </p>

        <h2>5. No Guarantees of Specific Search Engine Rankings</h2>
        <p>
          While Staten Island Software adheres to modern technical SEO best practices, semantic markup, and Core Web Vitals optimization, I do not guarantee specific numerical search rankings (e.g. "#1 on Google") on any search engine, as search algorithms and regional competitor dynamics are controlled solely by third-party search providers.
        </p>

        <h2>6. SMS / Text Messaging Terms &amp; Conditions</h2>
        <p>
          Staten Island Software / Jenkins HQ offers two optional, consent-based SMS/MMS messaging categories that you may separately opt into on our <a href="/jenkinshq/sms">SMS Opt-In page</a> or <a href="/contact">Contact form</a>:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Customer Service &amp; Transactional Updates:</strong> Responses to support requests, project consultations, order confirmations, digital delivery updates, and appointment reminders.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional Promotional &amp; Product Updates:</strong> Consent-based announcements of new software tools, product releases, and special offers (sent only if you separately check the promotional opt-in box).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Consent &amp; Confirmation:</strong> Opting in to SMS is completely optional and is never a condition of purchase. After opting in and once our carrier messaging campaign is active, you will receive a confirmation text message confirming your selected preferences.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Message Frequency &amp; Rates:</strong> Message frequency varies based on your active service requests or orders (and up to 4 messages per month for optional promotional updates). <strong>Message and data rates may apply.</strong> Consult your wireless carrier for plan details.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Opt-Out (STOP) &amp; Re-Subscribe (START):</strong> Reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to opt out of all Staten Island Software / Jenkins HQ text messages. You will receive one confirmation message and no further texts will be sent unless you reply <strong>START</strong> or submit a new opt-in.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Customer Support (HELP):</strong> Reply <strong>HELP</strong> to any text message for assistance, or email customer support at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a> (or <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Carrier Disclaimer &amp; Privacy:</strong> Wireless carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. View our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/jenkinshq/terms">Jenkins HQ SMS Terms</a> for full details on how we protect your mobile opt-in data.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Third-Party Services &amp; Dependencies</h2>
        <p>
          Certain web tools, communications, and automations interface with third-party providers (e.g., SignalWire, Netlify, Stripe, Google Cloud). Staten Island Software is not responsible for carrier delays, outages, or external vendor changes outside our control.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Customer Support &amp; Questions</h2>
        <p>
          For questions regarding these terms or customer support, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a> or submit an inquiry via the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-section {
    padding-top: 4.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem);
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-content {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 3rem;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal-content h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-content p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .legal-content li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-content {
      padding: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
